(LST2-95 — undocumented precision: in a grid, a `treating` clause binds to
 the ONE `each` clause it follows, not to the whole sentence. Here only
 the right-hand clause carries `treating 0 as 9`, and a 0 drawn from the
 left-hand list is left alone. LANGUAGE.md:3122 gives the syntax with the
 clause attached to a single `each`, but never says what happens to the
 other clauses of a grid.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-95.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   1-5
   1-9
   0-5
   0-9
)
To pair of a number called left and a number called right.
  print "{left}-{right}".

'pair' of each left from [1, 0] and each right from [5, 0] treating 0 as 9.
